WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.250
A drawing of a solid only shows some of its cubes.

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:05.830
The rest are hidden behind or underneath.

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:08.950
To count them all, slice the solid into layers.

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:11.510
Count one layer, then count the layers.

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:15.280
Counting only visible cubes can miss part of a solid.

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:18.540
Counting layer by layer is reliable, and it also answers

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:20.650
questions about which cubes are on the outside.

00:00:21.890 --> 00:00:25.610
A solid block is four cubes long, three cubes wide and

00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:26.660
two cubes high.

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:29.060
How many small cubes does it contain?

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:31.260
Pause and picture one layer.

00:00:34.990 --> 00:00:37.980
One layer is four by three, which is twelve cubes.

00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:39.970
There are two layers, so the block

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:41.580
contains twenty-four cubes.

00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:43.700
Half of them are in the bottom layer,

00:00:43.990 --> 00:00:45.760
including some that were hidden in the drawing.

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:47.840
Now a harder question.

00:00:48.490 --> 00:00:51.600
A three by three by three cube is painted all over,

00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:53.780
then cut into twenty-seven small cubes.

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:55.920
How many have no paint at all?

00:00:56.870 --> 00:00:59.200
Only a cube that touches no outside face.

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:01.860
Peel off the outer layer in every direction,

00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:04.540
and a single cube is left in the very centre.

00:01:04.910 --> 00:01:05.820
The answer is one.

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:08.210
You can sort all twenty-seven.

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:11.310
Eight corner cubes have three painted faces.

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:14.070
Twelve cubes along the edges have two.

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:17.160
One cube at the centre of each face has just

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:18.410
one painted side.

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:20.860
There are six faces, so there are six

00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:22.170
such cubes altogether.

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:24.250
One in the centre has none.

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:27.430
Eight, twelve, six and one make twenty-seven,

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:29.050
so nothing is missing.

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:32.530
Layers also handle uneven solids.

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:36.110
A corner staircase has nine cubes on the bottom layer,

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:39.790
four on the next and one on top: fourteen altogether.

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:42.310
Count each layer as it really is.

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:44.830
Slice the solid into layers.

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:46.350
Include the hidden cubes.

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:49.660
If you sort the cubes into types, check that the types

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:50.870
add up to the total.

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:54.960
Notebook challenge: a four by four by four cube is

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:57.030
painted and cut into small cubes.

00:01:57.560 --> 00:01:59.450
How many small cubes have no paint?
